8-test. The Ramanujan-Fourier coefficients `mu(q)/phi(q)` of the von Mangoldt function are classical (Hardy 1921) — re-derived here from S168 alone per the no-imports constraint. **Closure mode C**: T_Q does not break C-circular (computing it requires π(N) for the prefactor). The 79% remainder ‖chi_P − T_Q‖² is the bulk MP component. **Falsification status**: all four pre-stated falsifiers PASS. **Lean candidate**: the Hölder identity `mu(q) c_q(n)/phi(q) = mu(gcd)/phi(q/gcd)` is one-step character-theoretic, suitable for L1 queue. See experiments/constructions/ramanujan_spike_pointwise/. | 191 |
