    411	## §1. Composition Challenges
    412	
    413	A composition challenge says: build a single mathematical object whose
    414	*definition* uses two or more existing edges from EDGES.md, and whose
    415	*evaluator* produces a number you can compare to a baseline. Why this
    416	matters: edges are catalogued individually; their *interactions* are
    417	mostly unexplored. Composition is the cheapest source of genuinely new
    418	mathematical objects.
    419	
    420	**Discipline:** every composition target must produce code that runs.
    421	File under `experiments/constructions/<name>/`. Cite the edges by ID
    422	in `definition.md`. Failure mode is "duplicate of [composed-edge-X]"
    423	or "construction-incoherent" if the object isn't well-defined.
    424	
