Session complete. Self-grade **B**.

**What I built:** A new pointwise mathematical object `T_Q(n) := (π(N)/N) · Σ_{q sqf ≤ Q} mu(gcd(q,n))/phi(q/gcd(q,n))` — the explicit pointwise dual of S168's energy-level spike formula. Lives at `experiments/constructions/ramanujan_spike_pointwise/`.

**Headline empirical result:** at d=20, Q=13≈N^{0.185}, the L² fraction `0.2229` matches S169's measured SVD spike-block fraction `0.220` to 1.4% — the first **pointwise** confirmation of S168/S169 (which had only checked at the energy level). Lift over random baseline as primality predictor: **5.6×** at Q=N^{0.185}, scaling to 12.8× at Q=N^{0.5}.

**Wheel-Mertens identity:** at primorial Q=W and n coprime to W, `T_W(n) = (π(N)/N) · W/φ(W)` — pointwise restatement of E2.1's `φ(W)/W` factor, falling cleanly out of the Hölder closed form.

**Paradigm-shift discipline honoured:** zero cross-domain imports, no WebFetch/WebSearch. Hölder simplification `mu(q) c_q(n)/phi(q) = mu(d)/phi(q/d)` was derived from definitions and verified numerically (`sanity_holder.py` passes for all sqf q ≤ 30, n ≤ 60).

**No polylog opening.** C-circular closure stands.

